["I need to make 24 using 8, 5, 5, 9 with each number used once.\n\nLet me try different combinations.\n\n8, 5, 5, 9\n\nLet me think:\n- 9 - 5 = 4, 5 - ... \n- 8 * (9 - 5) - 5 = 8*4 - 5 = 32 - 5 = 27. No.\n- 8 * (9 - 5) + 5 = 37. No.\n- (9 - 5) * 5 - 8 = 20 - 8 = 12. No.\n- (9 + 5) * ... \n- 9 * 5 - 5 * 8 = 45 - 40 = 5. No.\n- 9 * 5 - 5 - 8 = 45 - 13 = 32. No.\n- (9 - 5) * (5 + ...) \n- 8 + 5 + 5 + 9 = 27. No.\n- 8 + 5 + 5 - 9 = 9. No.\n- 8 * 5 - 5 - 9 = 40 - 14 = 26. No.\n- 8 * 5 - 5 * 9 = 40 - 45 = -5. No.\n- 8 * 5 + 5 - 9 = 40 - 4 = 36. No.\n- 8 * 5 - (5 + 9) = 40 - 14 = 26. No.\n- 8 * 5 - (9 - 5) = 40 - 4 = 36. No.\n- (8 - 5) * (9 - 5) = 3 * 4 = 12. No.\n- (8 + 5) * ... \n- (9 - 8) * 5 * 5 = 25. No.\n- 9 * 8 / (5 - ...) \n- (5 + 5) * 9 - 8 = 90 - 8 = 82. No.\n- 5 * 5 - 9 + 8 = 25 - 1 = 24. Yes!\n\nLet me verify: 5 * 5 = 25, 25 - 9 = 16, 16 + 8 = 24. Yes!\n\nSo 5 * 5 - 9 + 8 = 24.\n"]